`asan_ubsan_agrees`.
The bound statements (`_disagrees_at_most`) use `Distribution.v`, which is not
translated, so they are *untranslated*: listed in `statements` as data, with no Lean
proposition (`Problem.denote?` is `none`, `<name>_untranslated`), neither provable
nor refutable. In particular they do not denote `False` (upstream's holds at
`b = 1`). Every other statement is a definition `S` with `denote? = some S`
(`<name>_eq`, by `rfl`).
